      "id": "AUD-013-DOC001",
      "severity": "low",
      "title": "Docs: audits README separator; Argon2id defaults undocumented; ambient getrandom in new crates; RELEASING lacks new gates",
      "legacyId": "L-04",
      "category": "DOC",
      "kind": "finding",
      "status": "open",
      "releaseBlocking": null,
      "detail": "1. `docs/audits/README.md` lists entry 12 with a different separator than entries 1–11 (cosmetic).\n2. `SECURITY_AUDIT.md:51` describes the Gordian password permit as Argon2id but not its strength: the pinned `bc-components` `Argon2idParams` stores only a 16-byte random salt and uses the `argon2` crate defaults (19 MiB memory, 2 iterations, 1 lane). This is the Blockchain Commons interoperability default and cannot be raised without breaking `ur:envelope` compatibility; users should be told that the container password must carry the entropy.\n3. `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md:42-45`: the Shamir entry says the module \"never selects an ambient RNG\"; the two new crates enable `getrandom` with browser features because `bc-envelope` draws salts/content keys itself (from WebCrypto). Accurate for Shamir, but the difference should be stated once.\n4. `RELEASING.md` does not mention `verify:wasm-producers` or `test:browser:selective` although both are now release gates in CI.\n\n### Informational\n\n- The in-commit `docs/audits/audit-12-2026-09-17.md` findings AUD-012-FUN001…AUD-012-DOC001 were verified as fixed: txid uses `concatBytes`; hex and Base64 both enforce the 16 MiB ceiling (probe: 17 MiB Base64 rejected); witness flag `0x02` rejected; clipboard fallback clears in `finally`; Shamir/SLIP-39 cleanup scopes present; recovery-workspace copy corrected. The two unused helpers and `createVaultChannel` are gone; `emptyHistory`/CSV/CompactSize duplicates are consolidated.\n- Committed WASM producers are the canonical `0.2.128` string for all five modules; `verify-wasm-producers` is in the verify chain.\n- Security greps over sources and all eight canonical artifacts: no `localStorage`/`sessionStorage`/`indexedDB`/cookies/`eval`/`new Function`/`innerHTML`/`XMLHttpRequest`/`WebSocket`/`EventSource`; one `fetch` site (`network-boundary/bounded-fetch.ts`); CSPs unchanged from audit 11 (offline tools `connect-src 'none'`, scanner vault `worker-src 'none'`, `sandbox=\"allow-scripts\"`), non-Dash connected builds pin provider origins.",
